meta {
  name: Webhooks
  seq: 5
}

docs {
  Protected webhook CRUD (org-aware when user has active org):
  - GET    /v1/webhooks
  - POST   /v1/webhooks
  - PUT    /v1/webhooks/:id
  - POST   /v1/webhooks/:id/rotate-token
  - PUT    /v1/webhooks/:id/pause
  - PUT    /v1/webhooks/:id/resume
  - DELETE /v1/webhooks/:id
  - GET    /v1/webhooks/:id/trades
  - DELETE /v1/webhooks/:id/trades/:tradeId
  - GET    /v1/webhooks/:id/pnl

  **Templates:** create (MT5/forex), create-indian (NSE/BSE equity), update, rotate-token, pause, resume, trades, cancel-trade, pnl.

  **Symbol conventions:**
  - `mt5_cloud` credential → webhook symbol `EURUSD`, `GBPUSD`, … (lots e.g. 0.01)
  - Indian credential → `RELIANCE`, `TCS`, … (integer share qty); credential `exchange` must match
  - Forex symbol + Indian cred → trade `rejected` / `invalid_symbol` (see Failure Modes setup)

  Full guide: repo `docs/broker-guide.md#symbol-conventions`
}
